{
  "$schema": "../../scenario.schema.json",
  "id": "response-schema/an-answer-that-fails-its-schema-is-not-tried-again",
  "title": "Under a retry policy, a constrained answer that fails its schema fails the turn at its first try, whether the model streams it or answers whole, and whether it is no JSON document, a refusal or an answer cut for room: a schema's error is never retryable, and the model is asked once",
  "rules": [
    "§6.7",
    "§6.4"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-6.7-079"
  ],
  "notes": "Python: providers/ai/json_schema.py ResponseSchemaError (a ProviderError, retryable False); channels/_ai_resilience.py retries only a retryable error. The agent's model.streaming false runs generate(), true its streaming method. The error's class is not read: its consequence, no other try under the policy, is.",
